    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15278" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ef-frĭco</span></b> , xi
				(<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 12</span></i>),
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to rub off</i> or <i>out</i> (post-Aug.  and very rare).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sordium enormem illuviem operose,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 105, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calices,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4</span></i>
			, p. 145, 31: spicas decerptas, Tert. l.
			l.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rubigo animorum effricanda est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 95, 37</span></i>
			.</div>
